# The ledgers are append-only sets of company names, written by workflow runs.
# Two runs that branch from the same commit both append at EOF — this workflow
# racing recent-seed-funding, or a scheduled run whose checkout predates a push
# that landed while it was running. Git sees two edits to the same trailing
# region and cannot auto-merge them, so the workflow's `git pull --rebase`
# stops with a conflict and the run's results are lost (the email has already
# gone out by then, so the companies are never recorded and resurface later).
#
# Union is the correct resolution for a set: keep the lines from both sides.
# It can leave duplicates when both runs found the same company, so the
# workflow dedups immediately after pulling, and run.sh dedups again on the
# next run.
seed-jobs/history/ledger.txt merge=union
recent-seed-funding/history/ledger.txt merge=union
